## One flexible mode in hybrid coordinates, transcribed from adcs-sim-core plant.rs (Flex, Body::flexible, deriv: the
## mode's part; the twin's asils.plant.deriv): J wdot + delta etadd = torques - w x (J w + h_rotors + delta etad),
## etadd + 2 zeta Omega etad + Omega^2 eta + delta . wdot = 0 (Hughes 1986, Spacecraft Attitude Dynamics, chapter 12).
## delta [sqrt(kg) m] couples the mode to the body; |delta|^2 is the inertia that takes part. Plain numbers in SI.
## The developer's transcription (S7.5), unsigned.
module flexmode

## The mode: whether there is one, its coupling delta, its natural frequency Omega [rad/s] and its damping ratio zeta.
record Flex
    on: bool
    delta: vec3[1]
    omega: real[1]
    zeta: real[1]
end

## The reduced inertia J - delta delta^T the body's equation divides by when the mode is on.
fn flex_reduced_inertia(inertia: mat3[1] in 0.001 .. 1, delta: vec3[1] in -0.05 .. 0.05) -> r: mat3[1]
    r = inertia
    for ia in 0 .. 3
        for ic in 0 .. 3
            r[ia][ic] = r[ia][ic] - delta[ia]*delta[ic]
        end
    end
end

## The mode's restoring and damping force on its coordinate, 2 zeta Omega etad + Omega^2 eta, which acts on the body
## through delta.
fn flex_pull(f: Flex, eta: real[1] in -1 .. 1, etad: real[1] in -1 .. 1) -> pull: real[1]
    pull = 2.0*f.zeta*f.omega*etad + f.omega*f.omega*eta
end
